equest() false during cooldown (no further effect); after cooldown -> half-open\",\n    \"half-open\": \"exactly one probe admitted; clean probe -> closed; failed probe -> open with a fresh cooldown\",\n    \"legalRate\": \"no failures -> never trips; sliding window prunes stale failures\",\n    \"deterministic\": \"injected clock; digest() reproducible\",\n    \"coexistsWith\": \"guardian-circuit-breaker (blocking-signal counting) - this adds the time dimension; does not relax SSRF/loop guard/approval\"\n  },\n  \"gates\": {\n    \"l05Tests\": {\n      \"command\": \"openclaw_runtime: run-vitest src/agents/rate-circuit-breaker.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"files\": 1,\n      \"tests\": 6,\n      \"failed\": 0\n    },\n    \"loopGuardRegression\": {\n      \"command\": \"openclaw_runtime: run-vitest tool-loop-detection.progress.test.ts rate-circuit-breaker.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"files\": 2,\n      \"tests\": 37,\n      \"failed\": 0\n    },\n    \"typecheckCore\": {\n      \"command\": \"openclaw_runtime: pnpm run tsgo:core\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    \"lintTouched\": {\n      \"command\": \"openclaw_runtime: run-oxlint rate-circuit-breaker.ts rate-circuit-breaker.test.ts\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    \"harnessValidate\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm harness validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-rate-circuit-breaker.md\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"result\": \"Spec is valid\"\n    },\n    \"harnessDryRun\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm harness run --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-rate-circuit-breaker.md --dry-run\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"result\": \"pass\"\n    },\n    \"commsReplay\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm run comms:replay\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0\n    },\n    \"commsCompare\": {\n      \"command\": \"pnpm run comms:compare\",\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"result\": \"all PASS, 0.00% delta\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"residual\": {\n    \"assembly\": \"The breaker core is provided; wiring it to a concrete provider/run call site is integration-layer work.\",\n    \"scope\": \"A boundary/limit, not a production default; does not relax SSRF/loop guard/approval and does not duplicate the existing outbound budget.\"\n  },\n  \"independentVerification\": {\n    \"executed\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"virtual-clock state-machine assertions + loop-guard regression\",\n    \"detail\": \"Tests drive the real breaker with an injected clock across legal-rate, trip, cooldown, half-open single-probe, recovery and window-pruning cases, and run alongside the tool-loop-detection regression to show the existing guard is unaffected. No separate second-agent verifier role was run.\",\n    \"separateVerifierAgent\": false\n  },\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finite-state\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"Closed/open/half-open state machine, deterministic under an injected clock.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"open-refuses\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"Requests are refused during the cooldown (no further effect) and only then move to half-open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"single-probe\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"Exactly one half-open probe is admitted; a second is refused while it is in flight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"recovery\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"A clean probe closes the breaker; a failed probe re-opens it with a fresh cooldown.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-false-trip\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"A purely legal rate never trips; sliding-window pruning prevents false trips in later legal windows.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-weakening\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"No SSRF/loop-guard/approval change; complements the existing blocking-signal guardian breaker and the outbound budget.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"clean-candidate-gates\",\n      \"status\": \"pass\",\n      \"note\": \"6 new + 31 loop-guard regression tests pass, tsgo:core 0, scoped lint 0, harness validate/dry-run pass, comms 0, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS verifiable.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"productLocks\": {\n    \"live_ready\": false,\n    \"product_approved\": false,\n    \"default_on\": false,\n    \"changed\": false\n  },\n  \"credentialScan\": {\n    \"files\": 3,\n    \"hits\": 0\n  },\n  \"notMeasured\": [\n    \"Live provider calls.\",\n    \"Wiring into a concrete provider/run call site.\",\n    \"A separate second-agent independent verifier role.\"\n  ],\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"pushed\": false,\n    \"pr\": null,\n    \"note\": \"Pushed with the evidence commit in the same session; see the branch's PR.\"\n  }\n}\n\r\n=== SHA\r\n985fd1b987c5b48dc7e69c512784465008cff242a06626c9ea27f24efb784e93  docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/l05-acceptance.json\n060f9502e17e3b7869ad81220c608aa7f01a6940cd72d7a233eb5e46e5aa8eee  docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/l05-rate-circuit-breaker.md\n8b01d13c5ab364d620d092154dea1f5a913e3380effea3b61bbec794691e5bd8  harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-rate-circuit-breaker.md\nc9fe9f1fdecb31bc9f2dee148fde45ff5f2f51e9132f1f4f16c13d157f517d29  openclaw_runtime/src/agents/rate-circuit-breaker.ts\nd6e73fa68719e77bca0546044ee91cfe5eeeaf1c43ef4d453f80072d32653394  openclaw_runtime/src/agents/rate-circuit-breaker.test.ts\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content openclaw_runtime/src/agents/resource-leases.ts -Raw'","aggregated_output":"/**\n * In-process workspace resource leases for agent tool concurrency.\n *\n * Several subagents can run in the same workspace at once. The lane-level\n * (`subagents.maxConcurrent`) and agent-level (`maxChildrenPerAgent`) limits do\n * not bound how many of them hit the same file tree or process table\n * simultaneously, so this manager adds a workspace-keyed budget with one FIFO\n * queue per (kind, key).\n *\n * It mirrors the Main-process `electron/services/resource-leases.ts` FIFO +\n * capacity + timeout structure that issue #162 wired into `terminal.run`, and\n * extends it to the workspace budget kinds from issue #167. Keys are opaque\n * strings: callers normalize them with `normalizeWorkspaceLeaseKey` so that\n * Windows case/slash variants and `realpath` aliases share one budget.\n *\n * The manager is ephemeral: it coordinates concurrent work inside a single\n * runtime process and does not persist queue state.\n */\nimport { realpathSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { createSubsystemLogger } from \"../logging/subsystem.js\";\n\nexport type ResourceLeaseKind =\n  | \"workspaceExec\"\n  | \"workspaceSearch\"\n  | \"workspaceWriter\"\n  | \"subtreeMutation\"\n  | \"fileMutation\";\n\nexport type ResourceLease = {\n  leaseKind: ResourceLeaseKind;\n  leaseKey: string;\n  queuedMs: number;\n  release: () => void;\n};\n\ntype ResourceLeaseMode = \"semaphore\" | \"path\";\n\nexport type ResourceLeaseOptions = {\n  /** Maximum time to wait for the lease. `<= 0` waits indefinitely. */\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000;\n\nconst RESOURCE_LEASE_CAPACITY: Record<ResourceLeaseKind, number> = {\n  workspaceExec: 2,\n  workspaceSearch: 2,\n  workspaceWriter: 1,\n  subtreeMutation: 1,\n  fileMutation: 1,\n};\n\n// Path kinds treat their key as a filesystem path and reject overlapping\n// subtrees; semaphore kinds treat their key as an opaque bucket.\nconst PATH_LEASE_KINDS = new Set<ResourceLeaseKind>([\"subtreeMutation\", \"fileMutation\"]);\n\nfunction leaseMode(kind: ResourceLeaseKind): ResourceLeaseMode {\n  return PATH_LEASE_KINDS.has(kind) ? \"path\" : \"semaphore\";\n}\n\n/**\n * Normalize a filesystem target into a stable lease key.\n *\n * Windows path comparison is case-insensitive and treats `/` and `\\` as the\n * same separator, so two spellings of the same workspace must map to one key.\n * Falls back to the resolved path when the target does not exist yet.\n */\nexport function normalizeWorkspaceLeaseKey(target: string): string {\n  let resolved = path.resolve(target);\n  try {\n    resolved = realpathSync.native(resolved);\n  } catch {\n    // Target may not exist yet; the resolved path is still a stable key.\n  }\n  return process.platform === \"win32\" ? resolved.replace(/\\\\/g, \"/\").toLowerCase() : resolved;\n}\n\nfunction isSameOrDescendantPath(candidate: string, ancestor: string): boolean {\n  if (candidate === ancestor) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  const base = ancestor.endsWith(\"/\") ? ancestor : `${ancestor}/`;\n  return candidate.startsWith(base);\n}\n\nfunction pathKeysConflict(a: string, b: string): boolean {\n  return isSameOrDescendantPath(a, b) || isSameOrDescendantPath(b, a);\n}\n\nexport class ResourceLeaseTimeoutError extends Error {\n  readonly code = \"RESOURCE_LEASE_TIMEOUT\";\n  readonly leaseKind: ResourceLeaseKind;\n  readonly leaseKey: string;\n  readonly queuedMs: number;\n  readonly timeoutMs: number;\n\n  constructor(params: {\n    leaseKind: ResourceLeaseKind;\n    leaseKey: string;\n    queuedMs: number;\n    timeoutMs: number;\n  }) {\n    super(\n      `Timed out waiting for ${params.leaseKind} lease (${params.leaseKey}) after ${params.timeoutMs}ms`,\n    );\n    this.name = \"ResourceLeaseTimeoutError\";\n    this.leaseKind = params.leaseKind;\n    this.leaseKey = params.leaseKey;\n    this.queuedMs = params.queuedMs;\n    this.timeoutMs = params.timeoutMs;\n  }\n}\n\ntype PendingRequest = {\n  id: number;\n  kind: ResourceLeaseKind;\n  key: string;\n  requestedAt: number;\n  timeoutMs: number;\n  resolve: (lease: ResourceLease) => void;\n  reject: (error: Error) => void;\n  timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null;\n};\n\ntype ActiveLease = {\n  id: number;\n  kind: ResourceLeaseKind;\n  key: string;\n};\n\nfunction sameBudget(a: PendingRequest | ActiveLease, b: PendingRequest | ActiveLease): boolean {\n  if (a.kind !== b.kind) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  return leaseMode(a.kind) === \"path\" ? pathKeysConflict(a.key, b.key) : a.key === b.key;\n}\n\nfunction normalizeTimeout(timeoutMs: number | undefined): number {\n  if (typeof timeoutMs !== \"number\" || !Number.isFinite(timeoutMs) || timeoutMs <= 0) {\n    return 0;\n  }\n  return Math.max(1, Math.floor(timeoutMs));\n}\n\nexport class ResourceLeaseManager {\n  private nextId = 1;\n  private readonly active = new Map<number, ActiveLease>();\n  private readonly pending: PendingRequest[] = [];\n  private readonly log = createSubsystemLogger(\"agents/resource-leases\");\n\n  acquire(\n    kind: ResourceLeaseKind,\n    key: string,\n    timeoutMs: number = DEFAULT_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_MS,\n  ): Promise<ResourceLease> {\n    const normalizedTimeout = normalizeTimeout(timeoutMs);\n    const id = this.nextId++;\n    const requestedAt = Date.now();\n    return new Promise<ResourceLease>((resolve, reject) => {\n      const request: PendingRequest = {\n        id,\n        kind,\n        key,\n        requestedAt,\n        timeoutMs: normalizedTimeout,\n        resolve,\n        reject,\n        timer: null,\n      };\n      if (normalizedTimeout > 0) {\n        request.timer = setTimeout(() => this.timeout(request), normalizedTimeout);\n      }\n      this.pending.push(request);\n      this.drain();\n    });\n  }\n\n  private drain(): void {\n    for (const request of this.pending.slice()) {\n      if (!this.pending.includes(request)) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (this.hasBlockingEarlierRequest(request)) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (!this.canGrant(request)) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      this.grant(request);\n    }\n  }\n\n  private hasBlockingEarlierRequest(request: PendingRequest): boolean {\n    for (const earlier of this.pending) {\n      if (earlier === request) {\n        return false;\n      }\n      if (sameBudget(earlier, request)) {\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  private canGrant(request: PendingRequest): boolean {\n    if (leaseMode(request.kind) === \"path\") {\n      return !this.hasActivePathConflict(request);\n    }\n    const capacity = RESOURCE_LEASE_CAPACITY[request.kind];\n    let activeCount = 0;\n    for (const lease of this.active.values()) {\n      if (lease.kind === request.kind && lease.key === request.key) {\n        activeCount += 1;\n      }\n    }\n    return activeCount < capacity;\n  }\n\n  private hasActivePathConflict(request: PendingRequest): boolean {\n    for (const lease of this.active.values()) {\n      if (sameBudget(lease, request)) {\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  private grant(request: PendingRequest): void {\n    if (!this.removePending(request)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    this.active.set(request.id, { id: request.id, kind: request.kind, key: request.key });\n    const queuedMs = Date.now() - request.requestedAt;\n    this.log.info(\"[resource-lease] acquired\", {\n      id: request.id,\n      leaseKind: request.kind,\n      leaseKey: request.key,\n      queuedMs,\n    });\n    let released = false;\n    request.resolve({\n      leaseKind: request.kind,\n      leaseKey: request.key,\n      queuedMs,\n      release: () => {\n        if (released) {\n          return;\n        }\n        released = true;\n        this.release(request.id, request.kind, request.key, queuedMs);\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  private release(id: number, kind: ResourceLeaseKind, key: string, queuedMs: number): void {\n    this.active.delete(id);\n    this.log.info(\"[resource-lease] released\", { id, leaseKind: kind, leaseKey: key, queuedMs });\n    this.drain();\n  }\n\n  private timeout(request: PendingRequest): void {\n    if (!this.removePending(request)) {\n      return;\n    }\n    const queuedMs = Date.now() - request.requestedAt;\n    this.log.warn(\"[resource-lease] timeout\", {\n      id: request.id,\n      leaseKind: request.kind,\n      leaseKey: request.key,\n      queuedMs,\n      timeoutMs: request.timeoutMs,\n    });\n    request.reject(\n      new ResourceLeaseTimeoutError({\n        leaseKind: request.kind,\n        leaseKey: request.key,\n        queuedMs,\n        timeoutMs: request.timeoutMs,\n      }),\n    );\n    this.drain();\n  }\n\n  private removePending(request: PendingRequest): boolean {\n    const index = this.pending.indexOf(request);\n    if (index < 0) {\n      return false;\n    }\n    this.pending.splice(index, 1);\n    if (request.timer) {\n      clearTimeout(request.timer);\n      request.timer = null;\n    }\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  /** Test-only: drop all active and pending leases. */\n  resetForTest(): void {\n    for (const request of this.pending) {\n      if (request.timer) {\n        clearTimeout(request.timer);\n        request.timer = null;\n      }\n    }\n    this.pending.length = 0;\n    this.active.clear();\n  }\n}\n\nconst resourceLeases = new ResourceLeaseManager();\n\nexport function isResourceLeaseTimeoutError(error: unknown): error is ResourceLeaseTimeoutError {\n  return error instanceof ResourceLeaseTimeoutError;\n}\n\n/** Test-only: clears lease state so suites do not leak capacity across cases. */\nexport function resetResourceLeasesForTest(): void {\n  resourceLeases.resetForTest();\n}\n\n/**\n * Acquire a workspace resource lease, run `fn`, then release it.\n *\n * `key` must already be normalized with `normalizeWorkspaceLeaseKey` so all\n * spellings of one workspace share a single budget.\n */\nexport async function withWorkspaceResourceLease<T>(\n  kind: ResourceLeaseKind,\n  key: string,\n  fn: (lease: ResourceLease) => Promise<T>,\n  options?: ResourceLeaseOptions,\n): Promise<T> {\n  const lease = await resourceLeases.acquire(kind, key, options?.timeoutMs);\n  try {\n    return await fn(lease);\n  } finally {\n    lease.release();\n  }\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
